==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Ranma Saotome (Cheer)''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Ranma is a good generalist backliner that does a solid generalist against her targeted traits. Her high range and [[Long Distance]] ability allow her to hit and [[Freeze]] [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] and [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] backliners such as [[Sunfish Jones]] and [[Director Kurosawah]]. Although freezing Dark enemies is a niche dominated by [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]], Ranma finds her place in it with her ability to hit the enemies Bombercat can't reach. Her high speed isn't as much of a detriment against black and angel type enemies usually have a lot of fast peons that keep the frontline solid, though she still runs the risk of getting caught by backliners (her 2 second backswing also helps with this issue). Her main knock against her targeted traits is her absolutely abysmal ability uptime of about '''22%'''. This restricts her use greatly as her freeze will not have a very high impact on the battle. Though the uptime is dismal, Ranma's LD AOE allows it to hit quite a lot of enemies, not just the backliners, so a 2 second freeze has a bigger impact than it would normally. One of the enemies Ranma does the best against is [[Winged Pigge]], as Ranma outranges its Omnistrike and a two second freeze on it can allow your fast damage dealers to hit it without getting weakened.

As a generalist, Ranma has solid backliner stats, which keep her usable as one, but she is outclassed by many other generalist ubers. However, her main generalist selling point is her [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]] and [[Immune to Surge|Surge Immunity]]. Wave and Surge Immune Units are hard to come by, and having a unit that can be immune to either or fulfills a few valuable niches. While she can only have one at a time, this is hardly important as stages with both wave and surge units are extremely uncommon. Against her targeted traits, Ranma is immune to the wave attacks of both [[Two Can]] and [[Youcan]], which allows her to stay alive a bit longer against them. It is important to bring strong tanks against these wavers because even if Ranma is unaffected by the waves, she will die quickly anyway if she is unsupported. Her average generalist stats allow her to hold her own against her non-target traits as well, especially against wave and surge enemies. Surge immunity is a much rarer niche, but also has less application. It makes Ranma into a strong pick against certain [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemies with powerful surges, but be wary of [[Shield]]s.

In summary, Ranma is a strong generalist that does a solid job against her traits, and fulfills a few rare and valuable niches, though she is unable to carry through stages and shines the most with proper defense and support.

